  (no tour)
  focus before Look (What was done = auth.terms): input#field-dtqacnz "[text field]"
  pressed: Look (What was done = auth.terms)
  main: Administration The trail The trail Every action this workspace records about itself. What it holds is who, what and when — never what anybody wrote. Look for From To What was done The start of an action name is enough — “auth.” finds every sign-in event. Who did it An account's identifier. Without the right to the whole trail, only your own events are answered. What kind of thing For example container, or legal_hold. Which one How it ended Any way Done Refused Failed Look Reading the trail is not itself recorded — a trail that grew by being read would bury what it is for. A refusal is recorded, and so is an export. Done Worth noticing auth.terms_agreed in the chain: 45 by Nora Newcomer · Oct 13, 2026, 8:23 AM about the account 01a133ee-16ed-7f5c-a707-9a02e23a612c terms_set_by became INSTALLATION terms_url became https://provider.example/legal/terms terms_version became 4 Done Worth noticing auth.terms_agreed in the chain: 35 by anna@consumer.example · Oct 13, 2026, 8:23 AM about the account 01a133e8-06d1-7511-8cba-4c65bc5a5a8f terms_set_by became INSTALLATION terms_url became https://provider.example/legal/terms terms_version became 4 Done Worth noticing auth.terms_agreed in the chain: 30 by Bert Consumer · Oct 13, 2026, 8:21 AM about the account 01a133eb-64d7-7acc-bdf8-c5fca3a53160 terms_set_by became INSTALLATION terms_url became https://provider.example/legal/terms terms_version became 4 Done Worth noticing auth.terms_agreed in the chain: 23 by Bert Consumer · Oct 13, 2026, 8:20 AM about the account 01a133eb-64d7-7acc-bdf8-c5fca3a53160 terms_set_by became INSTALLATION terms_url became https://provider.example/legal/terms terms_version became 3 Done Worth noticing auth.terms_agreed in the chain: 17 by anna@consumer.example · Oct 13, 2026, 8:20 AM about the account 01a133e8-06d1-7511-8cba-4c65bc5a5a8f terms_set_by became INSTALLATION terms_url became https://provider.example/legal/terms terms_version became 3 Does the record still hold? Every entry is chained to the one before it. Checking the chain over a period says whether anything has been altered or removed since. From To Check the chain Name a period first. Anchoring outside this database Once a day, the chain's end — the last entry's number and its hash — is written as a small file to a backup target of this workspace. That copy is what says something against somebody who could rewrite the whole database. Not anchored. The chain proves tampering inside the database only. Choose a target with object
